        {
          "id": 431633675,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I understand the \"generated field\" part of your comment, but for the\nparenthesized part, did you mean \"display the start and end of the\ncovered NSEC3 span\"?  I could do that, but:\n\n 1. That would require another wmem allocation (I am not sure if this is\n    a big deal or not) as we would need to extract the first label from\n    the owner name.\n\n 2. NSEC3 presentation should ideally match what is done for NSEC as\n    these two RR types essentially serve the same purpose.  In the case\n    of NSEC, the Next Domain Name field is printed in the RR subtree\n    (like in the current form of my MR) and *additionally* a `, next\n    domain name <name>` string is appended to the RR summary (next to\n    its owner name, type, and class).  The same effect could be achieved\n    here with the following change:\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/epan/dissectors/packet-dns.c b/epan/dissectors/packet-dns.c\nindex 293f7c83df..ffdb003c7f 100644\n--- a/epan/dissectors/packet-dns.c\n+++ b/epan/dissectors/packet-dns.c\n@@ -3285,6 +3285,7 @@ dissect_dns_answer(tvbuff_t *tvb, int offsetx, int dns_data_offset,\n         hash_value_base32hex[out_offset] = base32hex[group];\n       }\n       proto_tree_add_string(rr_tree, hf_dns_nsec3_hash_value, tvb, cur_offset, hash_len, hash_value_base32hex);\n+      proto_item_append_text(trr, \", next hashed owner name %s\", hash_value_base32hex);\n       cur_offset += hash_len;\n \n       rr_len = data_len - (cur_offset - initial_offset);\n```\n\nThis would result in:\n\n  - for NSEC:\n\n![nsec](/uploads/540429be9231994b587d46598035161b/nsec.png)\n\n  - for NSEC3:\n\n![nsec3](/uploads/337e4b05fff3d6bc706a1164d39f5baf/nsec3.png)\n\nThoughts?",
          "author": {
            "id": 2532284,
            "username": "kempniu",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michał Kępień",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b9aa7fb2b9db541938e4472389844b09b8aaaf438cdd905ee4e0d49839ccc2c8?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/kempniu"
          },
